Z||000001||88formula||01-28-2001||08:32 PM||||So you didn't like the Borla exhaust system I referred to you before huh? I have the Borla system and I must say that it is worth every penny. That same system for other cars costs much more than $500. There is one other exhaust system you can get for much cheaper but it does not compare to the Borla exhaust system in quality and sound and it won’t give you the power gains that the Borla exhaust system gives you. It is called the Ocelot performance exhaust system and it costs $270 with tips and $230 without tips. You can get it here <A HREF="http://www.fierostore.com/pegasus/index.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fierostore.com/pegasus/index.html</A>  <P>You could also just have a performance muffler put on like many other fiero owners here have done. To find out about that just do a search using the search function at the top of the page. There is a ton of information on this subject. <BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||GT Bastard||01-28-2001||08:39 PM||||No offense, but has anyone actually dyno'd a Borla system?||||reg||1
Z||000003||1FST2M6||01-29-2001||12:52 PM||||not sure what shops everyone is going to.. but the one on GT Bastards car cost me $180 the one on my GT was $200 cause of the polished tubing. the mufflers are $65-100 and their install should run $100ish. tips are from $40-65ea  and get 2.5" don't waste your time with 2.25" tubing. <P><BR>yeah what Jeff said... anyone have proof the Borla works?  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||1FST2M6||01-29-2001||01:00 PM||||you've got mail..   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||88formula||01-29-2001||06:07 PM||||The man to ask this question is the owner of Fieroparts <A HREF="http://www.fieroparts.com/." TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroparts.com/.</A>   The people I have talked to in person that have the Borla exhaust system mostly just says it sounds great and their gas mileage improved. Mine is not installed yet because it's going to go on my 3.4-liter engine, which is not done yet.<P>His wed site claims a 7 horsepower gain.<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||88formula||01-29-2001||06:12 PM||||Hey 1FST2M6, you never answered my question a while back about your car. How does your engine make more power with 0-ignition advance above 3200 rpm like you said? Most racing and street engines make more power with about thirty degrees of ignition timing. The more efficient ones like the GM LS1 like about 28. <P><BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||terryk||01-29-2001||06:40 PM||||I'm waiting for a Spintech 331SCS to arrive. <P>Single 2.5" in/dual 2" out, 13"x10"x4". I'll let you know how it works and sounds. $119.<P>If figured 10PSI of backpressure was just a bit too much and the Borla's and Flowmasters were too loud. Spintech was willing to work with me.<P>TK||||reg||1
Z||000008||1FST2M6||01-29-2001||09:48 PM||||i'm sorry.. i didn't see that post..   runnning at TDC the motor is at it's peak compression when the spark plug is ignited making the combustion more violent and stronger. I don't have any really detailed specifics just that it's at TDC at about 3500 and its a totally different car; at and above that range as you can see in the dyno charts. the SE was the same way. the Supra Turbo (87) the 300TT(94) i had all ran at TDC under full boost and they were happy about it and all had prety decent numbers. <BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstdyno_manymods.jpg" TARGET=_blank>www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstdyno_manymods.jpg</A> <P><BR>you'll be happy with spintech they are great units and have GREAT flow chart numbers!||||reg||1
